  "Question": "Data sets A and B have the same median. The first and third quartiles in A's box plot are 60 and 80, respectively, while those for B are 65 and 75. Which data set has a more concentrated middle 50% of the data? ( )",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Data set A",
    "B": "Cannot compare",
    "C": "Both are the same",
    "D": "Data set B"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A's interquartile range is $80-60=20$, and B's is $75-65=10$. B has a shorter box, so its middle 50% of the data is more concentrated.",
